    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.groupme.com/v3/bots/post",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ bot_id: '__GROUPME_BOT_ID__', text: '📝 New post draft + image ready for ' + $('Build Generator Prompt').first().json.scheduled_date + ' — review in the Dashboard.' }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.3,
      "position": [
        3300,
        240
      ],
      "id": "wf1-groupme-00000000000013",
      "name": "GroupMe Notify"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        3520,
        360
      ],
      "id": "wf1-respond-000000000014",
      "name": "Respond"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF1 — Nightly Generator (logic complete)\nRuns at 06:00 in TZ America/New_York. Also exposes the `fb-generate-now` webhook (verify the `x-webhook-secret: __N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET__` header — n8n redacts Authorization) that the Dashboard 'Generate Now' button calls with { scheduled_date }.\n\nPipeline: nightly path picks the next uncovered date within a 5-day horizon (duplicate guard); on-demand path uses the body's scheduled_date. Then: least-recently-used active subtopic (its pillar) → message bank + prompts → archetype → Anthropic generator → tolerant JSON parse → image prompt → Generate Image (OpenAI gpt-image-1, swappable) → decode → PUT upload to the PUBLIC fb-images bucket → set public image_url → insert fb_posts (copy_status/image_status='pending') → bump subtopic last_used_at/times_used → GroupMe.\n\nReplace `YOUR_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` and `__...__` placeholders with credentials/values on import. Keep `active:false` in the committed copy.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 460
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "wf1-note-00000000000015",
      "name": "About WF1"
    }
  ],
